t relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Workiva Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $4.0B market cap on $885M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years and +20% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Gross margins of 74% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $138M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -11.1% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.8%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 14% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 4.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 94% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9401757463685186},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short intere